---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { url } from '../consts';
---
<BaseLayout wide hero title="About" path="/about" description="Joe Neiman's story: flipping cars at 15, co-founding ACV Auctions through its $5B IPO, founding DealerClub, flying, and healing.">
  <div class="hero-full page-hero full-bleed">
    <img src={url('/assets/photos/joe-porsche-lean.jpg')} alt="Joe Neiman leaning on a white Porsche 911 with blue stripes" width="1800" height="1200" loading="eager" style="object-position: center 10%;" />
    <div class="hero-overlay"><span class="eyebrow">The story</span><h1>About</h1></div>
  </div>

  <!-- intro: lede beside the portrait -->
  <div class="split" data-rise>
    <div>
      <p class="lede">
    I grew up about 20 minutes outside of Albany, New York, in a pretty
    forgettable rural town. I learned the value of hard work early on through a
    combination of manual labor as a landscaper and construction worker and
    mechanic, as well as buying and selling cars in my parents' driveway starting
    at 15 years old.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure>
      <img src={url('/assets/photos/joe-portrait.jpg')} alt="Portrait of Joe Neiman" width="1066" height="1600" loading="eager" />
    </figure>
  </div>

  <!-- chapter: the first car -->
  <section class="chapter prose" data-rise>
    <h2>The first car</h2>
    <p>
      At 14 I started working summers at my uncle's small car repair shop, doing
      all the grunt tasks around the shop. The following summer he told me to buy
      an abandoned 1989 Honda Civic a customer had left behind. The price was the
      value of the car in scrap metal, which was $35. I spent about $200 putting
      used tires, a battery, and an exhaust on it, cleaned the car up, put an ad
      in the paper, and sold it for $900. That was a pivotal moment. I kept
      flipping cars out of my parents' driveway throughout the rest of high
      school, and by senior year I had a nice BMW 3 series and $20k in the bank,
      while my friends had to borrow $20 from their parents to go see a movie.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- chapter: the dealership, with the IDA commercial as the media moment -->
  <section class="chapter prose" data-rise>
    <h2>Lemons into lemonade</h2>
    <p>
      After college I moved back to Albany and started a dealership with a friend
      from high school. I knew better, but I ignored my gut feeling, and eleven
      months later he skipped town one night and left me about $100,000 in
      arrears. I had no choice other than to turn lemons into lemonade. Over the
      course of about four years I rebuilt myself and my business from $100,000 in
      the hole into leasing a former Chevy dealership facility, a dozen employees,
      selling 40-plus cars per month, and being a top rated seller on eBay.
    </p>
    <figure class="video-embed">
      <iframe src="https://player.vimeo.com/video/84672070" title="In Demand Auto commercial, 2014" loading="lazy" allow="fullscreen; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen></iframe>
    </figure>
    <p class="muted">The actual In Demand Auto commercial, 2014.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- chapter: ACV, with the record as a designed pair -->
  <section class="chapter prose" data-rise>
    <h2>ACV Auctions</h2>
    <p>
      ACV started on a yellow legal pad filled with notes and hand-drawn
      renderings of what a 20-minute online auction could look like, born out of
      the pain points and inefficiencies I had lived with as a dealer sourcing
      cars at physical auctions. On June 1, 2015 we ran our first auction in
      Buffalo, a high-mileage Mazda Tribute that drew bids from three local
      dealers and sold for around two thousand dollars. That was the start of
      something big. That October we won the 43North competition and its $1
      million first place prize, when my daughter was just six days old. We grew
      the company from three cofounders to over 2,000 teammates, raised
      approximately $300 million of venture capital, and went public on the
      Nasdaq in March of 2021 at a valuation over $5 billion. I consider my eight
      years growing ACV to be many lifetimes of professional careers, condensed
      into a whirlwind pressure cooker.
    </p>
    <div class="photo-pair">
      <figure>
        <img src={url('/assets/photos/43north-win.jpg')} alt="The ACV team celebrating on stage at 43North" width="920" height="627" loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>Winning 43North, October 2015.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <img src={url('/assets/photos/ipo-day-nasdaq.jpg')} alt="Joe Neiman at the Nasdaq podium on ACV's IPO day" style="object-position: center 30%;" width="568" height="696" loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>IPO day at the Nasdaq, March 2021.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- chapter: DealerClub -->
  <section class="chapter prose" data-rise>
    <h2>DealerClub</h2>
    <p>
      In 2023 I started again with DealerClub, the wholesale auction rebuilt
      around reputation, where honest sellers get rewarded for being honest.
      Cars Commerce acquired it three months after we went live commercially.
    </p>
  </section>

  <blockquote class="pullquote" data-rise>
    <p>&ldquo;Cars are not commodities. They aren't bushels of wheat.&rdquo;</p>
    <cite>Joe Neiman</cite>
  </blockquote>

  <section class="chapter prose" data-rise>
    <p>
      Trust and transparency, the slogan I have carried since the In Demand Auto
      days, was the same idea DealerClub was built on in 2023.
    </p>
  </section>

  <figure class="media-band full-bleed" data-rise>
    <img src={url('/assets/photos/nada-cars-commerce.jpg')} alt="Joe Neiman and the team at the NADA Show announcement that DealerClub is now part of Cars Commerce" width="1600" height="1200" loading="lazy" />
    <figcaption>The announcement at the NADA Show.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <!-- chapter: health -->
  <section class="chapter" data-rise>
    <h2 class="prose">The health story</h2>
    <p class="two-col">
      I'm an open book on this one. The colitis started at 19 and continued on
      and off for more than 15 years. I ran down every single rabbit hole
      conceivable to try and resolve it. My experience and my truth is that my
      disease was caused by excessive stress and anxiety, which is the space I
      lived in secretly for most of my life. Until I actually learned how to
      identify that and manage it and restore balance to my body, nothing would
      work. I have actually experienced instantaneous healing, where active
      symptoms resolved themselves overnight after I was able to reframe my
      disease in my mind. I'm not a doctor and this isn't medical advice. It's
      what happened to me.
    </p>
    <div class="photo-pair natural">
      <figure>
        <img src={url('/assets/photos/backcountry-ski.jpg')} alt="Joe Neiman in backcountry ski gear on a mountain" loading="lazy" />
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <img src={url('/assets/photos/ski-selfie.jpg')} alt="Joe Neiman giving a thumbs-up on the ski slope" loading="lazy" />
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <blockquote class="pullquote" data-rise>
    <p>&ldquo;Everything needs a soul. People are not robots.&rdquo;</p>
    <cite>Joe Neiman</cite>
  </blockquote>

  <!-- chapter: flying -->
  <section class="chapter" data-rise>
    <h2 class="prose">Flying</h2>
    <p class="prose">
      In the past five years I have gone from zero to 1,000-plus hours, flying
      highly complex aircraft, with a commercial instrument multi-engine pilot
      certificate. I own multiple airplanes, but the two extremes are a Waco
      YMF-5 biplane and a Piaggio Avanti P180. Flying my entire family from
      Florida to New York in three hours, at altitudes above the airliners, feels
      like a superpower. Being a true adult student has taught me a lot about
      self-discipline, and I take it seriously and respect the risks and decision
      making that come with it.
    </p>
    <div class="gallery-row">
      <figure>
        <img src={url('/assets/photos/waco.jpg')} alt="Red Waco YMF-5 biplane in a hangar" loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>The Waco YMF-5.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <img src={url('/assets/photos/avanti.jpg')} alt="Piaggio Avanti P180 in a hangar" loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>The Piaggio Avanti P180.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <img src={url('/assets/photos/flying-headset.jpg')} alt="Joe Neiman at altitude, headset on" loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>At altitude.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <blockquote class="pullquote" data-rise>
    <p>Any fool with too much money can buy a Bugatti, but you're still stuck
    driving from one traffic light to the next.</p>
    <cite>Joe Neiman</cite>
  </blockquote>

  <!-- closer: what I read, as the designed end of the page -->
  <section class="band band-gold closer-band full-bleed" data-rise>
    <div class="band-inner">
      <span class="eyebrow">What I read</span>
      <blockquote>
        I've read hundreds of books in my adult life. I try to be a student of lives
        well lived, and try to apply the lessons learned to my life.
      </blockquote>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn" href={url('/contact')}>Contact</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
